# Copy to .env and fill in. Both keys are free tier — no billing account and no
# card is required for either.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed.


# --- Runtime: drafting -------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini writes the reply, grounded in the retrieved SOP. Required only for live
# drafting; classification, routing, the Streamlit queues and their SOP panes run
# without an API key.
#
# Get one: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Free-tier rate limits apply and will occasionally fire during a full eval
# sweep. That is expected behaviour, not a defect: a failed draft escalates the
# item to the human queue with its SOP attached, rather than degrading into a
# lesser reply. See BUILD.md S5.8.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL FALLBACK KEYS. Free-tier drafting quota is a DAILY budget, not a
# per-minute one: once a key returns 429 it keeps returning 429 for hours, which
# is long enough to stop an eval sweep or a live demo dead. Add a second key from
# a different Google account and the drafter rotates to it automatically on rate
# limit, then continues from there.
#
# Rotation fires ONLY on a rate limit. A timeout or a withdrawn model is not a
# quota problem, so retrying it on another key would spend two keys on the same
# failure. When every key is exhausted the call fails exactly as it would with
# one key, and drafting availability is still reported honestly -- the fallback
# buys headroom, it does not hide the limit.
#
# Leave blank if you only have one key; the pipeline behaves identically.
GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
GEMINI_API_KEY_3=

# --- Evaluation: groundedness judge ------------------------------------------
# Groq is the primary judge for the groundedness check. Eval-time only — not
# needed to run the pipeline or the demo.
# The judge defaults to Compound Mini for higher free-tier token throughput. Its
# external tools are disabled so it judges only the supplied SOP evidence.
#
# Get one: https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# A different model family from the drafter on purpose: a model must not be
# scored on its own output (BUILD.md S6.4).
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Build-time: corpus and email generation ---------------------------------
# Used only by scripts/ when regenerating the SOP corpus or the synthetic email
# set. Both outputs are frozen and committed, so a grader reproducing the
# results never needs this key.
OPENAI_API_KEY=


# --- Optional settings -------------------------------------------------------
# Model identifiers, pinned so results are reproducible. Free-tier model rosters
# rotate, so the identifier actually used is recorded in eval/results/ too.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# GROQ_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# GROQ_JUDGE_MODEL=groq/compound-mini

# Streamlit workflow events are printed to the terminal at INFO level by default.
# Set this to DEBUG, WARNING, ERROR or CRITICAL to change their verbosity.
# TRIAGE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Seed for splits, generation and training. Recorded in eval/results/.
# SEED=42
